  }, {
    "id" : "13bbfdaa",
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "content" : [ {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : "Create the About page artifact at route "
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : "/about",
      "styles" : {
        "code" : true
      }
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : " in the web source tree (new — the repository currently has no web layer; place it alongside where the landing page lives once Task 2 establishes it, or in the conventional static-page location for the chosen web setup). The page renders an "
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : "<h1>",
      "styles" : {
        "code" : true
      }
    }, {
      "type" : "text",
      "text" : "/heading with the text \"About\" followed by a few fixed body paragraphs describing who the company is and what it does, wrapped in the same layout chrome and stylesheet as the rest of the landing site. The route must be served to unauthenticated visitors. The content is a constant in the artifact — do NOT introduce an entity, a content store, a CMS hook or an editing path; the spec's Data model section rules that out explicitly."
    } ]
  }, {
